The task description tells you which LLR needs a test case and provides the SUITE parent ID. Create ONE CASE_LLR for that specific LLR.

IMPORTANT: Every LLR gets its OWN dedicated CASE_LLR. Do NOT add this LLR to an existing CASE node's trace_to. Always create a new CASE_LLR.

graph_add_node:
   - node_type = CASE_LLR
   - parent_id = SUITE node ID (from task description)
   - content = unit test specification: function/method under test, input values, expected output, edge cases to cover
   - title = 3–5 words (e.g. 'Token Validation Unit Test')
   - trace_to = [the single LLR node ID this case verifies]

